  "prs": [
    {
      "number": 14587,
      "title": "[mediaqueries-5] Add application display-mode and concurrent values #14125",
      "url": "https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/14587",
      "author": "kyerebo",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-16T19:47:04Z",
      "hint": "unknown",
      "release": "⏳ 未リリース",
      "body": "Adds specification text for a `display-mode: application` value, along with removing the mutual exclusivity of `display-mode` values which caused issues with accurate `display-mode` detection.\n\nWhen a developer is querying for `display-mode: standalone`, and the user enters fullscreen, `display-mode: standalone` stops matching. The query now instead matches `display-mode: fullscreen`. This mutual exclusivity of `display-mode` values made for inconsistent signals and unpredictable behavior for developers to work with.\n\nThis change adds a new, stable signal for being in an application context `display-mode: application`.\nSupplementally fix matching behavior to be independent per value definition and allow more than one value to match at a time.\n\nReview discussion at https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14125",
      "files": [
        "mediaqueries-5/Overview.bs (+24 -15)"
      ],
      "filesTotal": 1
    },
    {
      "number": 14611,
      "title": "[css-contain-2] Define skipped media playback behavior (#6468)",
      "url": "https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/14611",
      "author": "hjanuschka",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-18T16:22:11Z",
      "hint": "unknown",
      "release": "⏳ 未リリース",
      "body": "Spec edits for the [2021 CSSWG resolution](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/6468#issuecomment-887634200) on media playback in skipped subtrees.\n\n- Media elements skipped via `content-visibility: hidden` keep playing with audio suppressed (without changing `muted`/`volume`), queued events are deferred until unskipped, and state queries reflect the live playback state.\n- Applies through nested `iframe`s; picture-in-picture presentation outside the skipped contents is exempt.\n- Explicitly scoped to `content-visibility: hidden` only: contents skipped via `content-visibility: auto` are unaffected, so off-screen audio keeps playing.\n\nCloses #6468",
      "files": [
        "css-contain-2/Overview.bs (+28 -0)"
      ],
      "filesTotal": 1
    }
  ],
